      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T06:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@Eric\n\u003e\u003eCould we do this reversely that we skip GPIO initialization if eSPI is configured?\nThis is the device tree source file. I don\u0027t see a approach to conditionally exclude the \u0026alt0_gpio_no_spip when eSPI is configured.\n@Andrew\nYes, this is also what the Zephyr community strongly suggests during the code review for the pinctrl driver refactor.\nSee also the principle in the [doc](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/hardware/pinctrl/index.html) \n```\nIt is discouraged to add pin configuration defaults in pre-defined nodes. In general, pin configurations depend on the board design or on the peripheral working conditions, so the decision should be made by the board. \n```\nWe might also remove the def-io-conf-list from the SoC default and move it to the board\u0027s folder which uses eSPI interface latter like what I did in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "fc7537c9_1890bb5a",
      "revId": "bd252b2503aa80fdb5af48b213adb41f52bcfc3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
